Root cause:
The bug in BoolField was due to an incorrect implementation of the `toExternal` method, which erroneously returned "false" for all documents when the binary value of the indexable field was null. The logic did not properly handle cases where the binary value could be absent but a string value could still exist, resulting in an inability to correctly interpret and represent boolean field values. The fix involved revising the conditionals in the `toExternal` method to ensure that if the binary value is null, it checks for a string value before deciding to return null.
